+// (review 95699). `release_locus_record` is the ONE mint for the release shape: it derives spine and
+// locus from (base_root, revision) together, so a caller that mints cannot pair a locus with a
+// revision it was not minted for. `helper_release_locus_record` is the one mint for the root-helper
+// snapshot shape under a HelperLocus; it likewise derives the directory from the revision it names.
+// The type's constructor stays open (a record is a plain carrier), so the guarantee is "these two
+// folds are the sanctioned mints; every release/helper install obtains its locus through one of them,"
+// NOT "a mismatched record is unwritable" -- the constructor is public. Stated at that rung per
+// gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder: the reported rung equals the rung the code establishes.
 type ReleaseLocus {
